{"task":"transcribe","language":"english","duration":35.619998931884766,"text":"A warrior has fallen onto a shield and props himself up on one arm, wounded. Beside him lie a broken sword and a trumpet. He is a Gaul, a Celt, you can tell from the twisted metal ring around his neck, the mustache with no beard, and the tangled hair. The statue is a marble copy of a lost bronze made in Pergamon, in Asia Minor, around 230 B.C., to celebrate a victory over the Gauls. In 1797, Napoleon took to Paris. It came back to Rome in 1816. The poet Byron wrote a poem about it.","words":[{"word":"A","start":0,"end":0.5600000023841858},{"word":"warrior","start":0.5600000023841858,"end":1.0199999809265137},{"word":"has","start":1.0199999809265137,"end":1.4600000381469727},{"word":"fallen","start":1.4600000381469727,"end":1.7599999904632568},{"word":"onto","start":1.7599999904632568,"end":2.0999999046325684},{"word":"a","start":2.0999999046325684,"end":2.440000057220459},{"word":"shield","start":2.440000057220459,"end":2.7200000286102295},{"word":"and","start":2.7200000286102295,"end":3.140000104904175},{"word":"props","start":3.140000104904175,"end":3.4200000762939453},{"word":"himself","start":3.4200000762939453,"end":3.799999952316284},{"word":"up","start":3.799999952316284,"end":4.119999885559082},{"word":"on","start":4.119999885559082,"end":4.239999771118164},{"word":"one","start":4.239999771118164,"end":4.559999942779541},{"word":"arm","start":4.559999942779541,"end":4.760000228881836},{"word":"wounded","start":5.579999923706055,"end":5.579999923706055},{"word":"Beside","start":6.78000020980835,"end":6.78000020980835},{"word":"him","start":6.78000020980835,"end":7.079999923706055},{"word":"lie","start":7.079999923706055,"end":7.320000171661377},{"word":"a","start":7.320000171661377,"end":7.880000114440918},{"word":"broken","start":7.880000114440918,"end":7.880000114440918},{"word":"sword","start":7.880000114440918,"end":8.180000305175781},{"word":"and","start":8.180000305175781,"e